## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where Canvas A2UI users could make the CLI or agent tool buffer an arbitrarily large JSONL file before validation.

## Why This Change Was Made

Canvas now reads JSONL files through one extension-owned 8 MiB bounded reader. The bound leaves room under the 25 MiB Gateway frame limit for JSON escaping and RPC metadata, and it applies to both `--jsonl` and `jsonlPath`.

## User Impact

Oversized A2UI files fail before unbounded buffering, while valid files near the limit continue through normal validation and node invocation.

## Evidence

- Real CLI before/after: the baseline read an 8,388,609-byte file and reached JSON parsing; the patched CLI rejected the same file at the size boundary.
- Legitimate large case: an 8,386,678-byte valid A2UI payload passed file reading and validation, then reached the Gateway connection boundary.
- `pnpm exec vitest run extensions/canvas/src/a2ui-jsonl-file.test.ts extensions/canvas/src/cli.test.ts extensions/canvas/src/tool.test.ts`: 38 tests passed.

```text
$ pnpm openclaw nodes canvas a2ui push --node proof-node --jsonl <proof-root>/oversized.jsonl --url ws://127.0.0.1:1 --token [redacted]
before: Invalid A2UI JSONL: line 1 ... is not valid JSON
after: A2UI JSONL file exceeds 8388608 bytes: <proof-root>/oversized.jsonl

$ pnpm openclaw nodes canvas a2ui push --node proof-node --jsonl <proof-root>/valid-large.jsonl --url ws://127.0.0.1:1 --token [redacted]
fixture: validBytes=8386678
result: gateway closed ... Gateway target: ws://127.0.0.1:1
```

<details>
<summary>proof-live.ts</summary>

```ts
import { mkdtemp, open, writeFile } from "node:fs/promises";
import os from "node:os";
import path from "node:path";
import { MAX_A2UI_JSONL_FILE_BYTES } from "./extensions/canvas/src/a2ui-jsonl-file.js";

const root = await mkdtemp(path.join(os.tmpdir(), "openclaw-canvas-proof-"));
await writeFile(
  path.join(root, "openclaw.json"),
  JSON.stringify({ plugins: { entries: { canvas: { enabled: true } } }),
);

const valid = JSON.stringify({
  surfaceUpdate: {
    surfaceId: "main",
    components: [
      {
        id: "text",
        component: {
          Text: {
            text: { literalString: "x".repeat(MAX_A2UI_JSONL_FILE_BYTES - 2048) },
          },
        },
      },
    ],
  },
});
await writeFile(path.join(root, "valid-large.jsonl"), valid);

const oversizedPath = path.join(root, "oversized.jsonl");
const oversized = await open(oversizedPath, "w");
await oversized.truncate(MAX_A2UI_JSONL_FILE_BYTES + 1);
await oversized.close();

console.log(
  JSON.stringify({
    root,
    validBytes: Buffer.byteLength(valid),
    oversizedBytes: MAX_A2UI_JSONL_FILE_BYTES + 1,
  }),
);
```

</details>

